K8 is divided into 2 parts ->Control Plane and Data Plane
Control plane is controlling the actions and Data plane is executing the actions
Control plane includes components like API Servers , ETCD , Controller manager and Cloud Controller manager (CCM). (Master component)
Data Plane includes kubelet , kubeproxy , container runtime. (Worker node components)
What happens when container is created in Docker and what happens when pod is created in K8 
Container Runtime = A container runtime is the software component responsible for running and managing containers on a host operating system . provides executing environment for containers to run

Below comparison for Docker and K8 to demonstrate K8 arch with docker components as example
Docker 
Container runtime – In docker it is called as Docker shim , this docker shim and docker engine is responsible for running the containers It is used to act like bridge between k8 and docker , in earlier version of Kube , Docker was default container runtime.
Networking – Default is Bridge Networking

K8
Master Node and Worker Node – There might multiple master and multiple worker nodes , 
Container Runtime – Kube supports Containerd ,CRI-O , also supports Docker Shim –these are container runtimes which implements k8s container interface , So it is responsible for running our containers , it provides executing environment for containers to run
Kubelet – Responsible for running the pods and creation of pods or the pod should should always run , if not since k8 have auto scaling technology it will inform api servers to make necessary actions using k8s control plane	
Networking - Kubeproxy – Every pod / container creating is allocated with Ip Address and load balancing capabilities , So it is useful for generating IP address , load balancing , uses IP tables on linux machines for networking related configurations.
Above 3 components will be in Worker nodes.
So , This Worker node / Data plane is responsible for Running our Applications
Control Plane/Master Node components
API Server – The purpose of API Server is to expose K8 to external world which takes requests from external world and this is heart of k8 , Previously discussed worked nodes are internal to K8. 
Scheduler – The purpose of scheduler is to schedule pods/resources on k8 , whose will decide where this needs to be schedule -> it is API Servers.
etcd - Backup service which backups , store entire production cluster information. It is key value store in which entire cluster information stored as objects or key-value pairs
